/-!
# Stacks Tag 01WB: locally projective is locally H-projective

A morphism of schemes is *locally projective* when its base is covered by opens over each of
which it is a closed immersion into the projective bundle `𝐏(ℰ)` of a quasi-coherent module of
finite type, and *locally H-projective* when its base is covered by opens over each of which it
is a closed immersion into `ℙⁿ`. The second condition visibly implies the first, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallyProjective_of_isLocallyProjectiveMorphism`. **This file proves the
converse**, and hence the equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 01WB].

## The source's proof, and where each step is

The source argues: over an affine open `U = Spec R` of the base, `ℰ` is `M~` for a finite type
`R`-module `M` ([Stacks, Tag 01PB]); a choice of generators `x₀, …, xₙ` of `M` gives a surjective
graded `R`-algebra map `R[X₀, …, Xₙ] → Sym_R(M)`; so the induced morphism
`𝐏(ℰ) → ℙⁿ_R` is a closed immersion ([Stacks, Tag 01N0]); hence `f⁻¹(U)` is a closed subscheme of
`ℙⁿ_U` over `U`.

That is exactly the route taken here, read on the chart of the projective bundle over the affine
open. The chart of `𝐏(ℰ) = Proj_U(Sym(ℰ))` over an affine open `V` is `Proj Γ(V, Sym(ℰ))` and is
the inverse image of `V`, by the defining property of the relative homogeneous spectrum; so no
base change of the projective bundle — [Stacks, Tag 01O3], which is carried by
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjBaseChangeIso` but only for a graded algebra supplied
together with an identification of it with a pullback, as `Sym(ℰ)` is not —
is needed, and the source's surjection is the surjection of *that* graded ring of sections by a
polynomial ring. The geometry is
`Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.isProjectiveMorphism_pullback_snd_of_degreeOne` of the
sibling file; what this file supplies is its three algebraic hypotheses for `Sym(ℰ)`.

* **Generation in degree one over the degree-zero part** is
  `Stacks.SymGraded.isGeneratedInDegreeOneAt_schemeSheafGradedAlgebra`.
* **The degree-zero part is the image of the structure map.** Over an affine open the
  sheafification unit of the sectionwise symmetric algebra is bijective
  (`Stacks.SymGraded.bijective_sheafifyUnit_app_of_isAffineOpen`), and `Sym⁰_R(M)` is the span of
  `1`, so a degree-zero section is a multiple of the unit.
* **The degree-one part is generated by finitely many elements**, which is where Tag 01PB is
  spent: `Γ(ℰ, V)` is a finite `Γ(X, V)`-module by
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections`, `Sym¹_R(M)` is the image of `M`, and
  the unit carries a generating family of the one to a generating family of the other.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.exists_smul_oneG` and `exists_sum_smul_ιG`: the algebraic
  input — the degree-zero piece of a symmetric algebra is the multiples of the unit, and the
  degree-one piece is spanned by the images of a generating family of the module.
* `Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.exists_smul_one_eq`,
  `exists_fin_span_piece_one`, `exists_strHom_eq` and `exists_fin_span_grading_one`: those two
  facts for the sections of `Sym(E)` over an affine open, and then for the degree-zero and
  degree-one parts of the graded ring of sections.
* `Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.isProjectiveMorphism_pullback_snd_of_isProjective` and
  `isProjectiveMorphism_morphismRestrict_of_isProjective`: **a projective morphism is H-projective
  over every affine open of its base**, as a base change and as a restriction.
* `Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.isLocallyProjectiveMorphism_of_isLocallyProjective`:
  **the implication (1) ⟹ (2) of [Stacks, Tag 01WB]**.
* `Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.isLocallyProjective_iff_isLocallyProjectiveMorphism`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 01WB]**, both implications.

## Implementation notes

**The covering produced is indexed by pairs.** `AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocallyProjective` gives
opens `Uᵢ` of the base over which `f` is projective, and projectivity gives H-projectivity only
over the *affine* opens of each `Uᵢ`; so the covering witnessing
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocallyProjectiveMorphism` is indexed by a pair `(i, V)` with `V` an affine
open of `Uᵢ`, its member being the image of `V` in the base. Those images cover because the
affine opens of each `Uᵢ` cover `Uᵢ` and the `Uᵢ` cover the base. The restriction of `f` to the
image is `(f ∣_ Uᵢ) ∣_ V` by `AlgebraicGeometry.morphismRestrictRestrict`, and no affineness of
the image is used.

**The two spellings of the ring of functions on an open meet in this file, and `rw` does not
survive it.** The module structure on the sections of the sectionwise symmetric power is over
`Stacks.SymGraded.siteRing`, the `RingCat`-valued forgetful image of `Γ(X, V)`, while the
statements below are over `Γ(X, V)`; the two are definitionally but not reducibly equal, so a
goal mentioning both is not type-correct at `implicit` transparency and `rw` fails on patterns
that are present. The sum over the sheafification unit is therefore moved across it by naming
the unit as an honest `Γ(X, V)`-linear map (`F` in
`Stacks.LocallyProjectiveHProjective.exists_fin_span_piece_one`), after which `map_sum` and
`map_smul` apply in one spelling; the same remark is recorded in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafSymmetricAlgebra.ProjectiveSpaceMorphism`.

**Three notes elsewhere in the tree asserted that this was blocked, and are corrected by this
file.** The implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiProjective.HProjective` said the converse "needs a surjection
`𝒪_U^{n+1} ↠ ℰ` … whose input — a homomorphism of sheaf symmetric algebras produced from a
homomorphism of modules — nothing in the library constructs"; those of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Proper.Projective` said "01WB is exactly the missing
step"; and `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Projective.Basic` said that
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective` is not proved to imply
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocallyProjective` because the base change of the projective bundle along
the inclusion of an open is unavailable. No homomorphism of sheaf symmetric algebras and no base
change of the bundle is used: the chart over an affine open *is* an absolute `Proj`, and the
surjection is of graded rings.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WB)
